+# What the congressional recommendation returns counted
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 UTC source review. B129 / PD03–PD04, supporting PD01–PD02. This check follows the December 2008 update cited by the House majority staff and the earlier scope discussions. It adds primary records from two other recipients of the inquiry. The USDA OIG response gives an exact request date and describes a separate financial-office return. EPA OIG documents a supplemental search outside its initial tracking-system report. These are concrete checks to apply when locating DOT's underlying return and determining whether it covered the FAA referral. [House methodology, physical p. 5](https://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/200901Majority_Report.pdf#page=5) · [USDA update, physical p. 13](https://www.governmentattic.org/6docs/USDAoUnpubCongRpts_2008-2010.pdf#page=13) · [EPA revised methodology, physical pp. 58–59](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=58)
+
+## USDA's response and the House table
+
+| Record and locator | Recorded scope and values |
+| --- | --- |
+| USDA letter dated **February 21, 2008**, physical p. 16, sorted text lines 21–26 and 37–42 | Describes the December 7 request as **January 1, 2001, to the present** and reports **3,354** recommendations in **583** audit reports issued through **December 31, 2007**. The letter gives a separately granted response extension to **February 22**. |
+| USDA February attachment, physical p. 19, lines 3–27 | Gives a **January 11, 2008** status date and **732** recommendations, split **128** pending management decision and **604** pending final action. Its detailed reporting subsets are **36** past the management-decision interval and **361** past the final-action interval. Within the latter, **39** were considered to have achieved final action by the reporting agency and awaited the Chief Financial Officer's review. |
+| USDA OIG December update, physical p. 13, lines 3–11 and 21–35 | Identifies an **e-mail request dated December 15, 2008** and a **December 15, 2008** data cutoff. Its retrospective first-period count is **3,353** in **583** reports. It reports **3,610** recommendations issued through the updated date and **55** pending management decision. The response says the Office of the Chief Financial Officer would provide a separate chart for items with management decisions that were still awaiting implementation. |
+| USDA December chart, physical p. 14, lines 9–22 | Reports **0, 4, 4, 3, 1, 0, 9, 34** pending management decision by year for **2001–2008**. The eight issued-recommendation rows sum to **3,610**, including **257** for 2008. The 2001–2007 rows sum to **3,353**. |
+| January 2009 House majority staff appendix, physical p. 15, printed p. 11, sorted line 17 | The USDA row under **Total Open Recs.** gives **5, 7, 26, 26, 52, 111, 150, 370** by issue year, summing to **747**. The separate issued count is **3,610**. The methodology describes seeking data through year-end and receiving partial or full responses. |
+
+Preserve **3,354** and **3,353** with their document versions. Preserve the USDA OIG table's **55** and the House row's **747** with their headings and dates. The arithmetic difference is **692**. The actual December financial-office return and the House's compilation worksheet remain unacquired. A split of the House total into **55** OIG items plus **692** from the financial office is an untested hypothesis. The shared **3,610** total also leaves a year-level problem. The House gives **370** open items issued in 2008, while the December 15 USDA table gives **257** issued in 2008. If both values cover the same population and cutoff, the open count would exceed the issued count by **113**. The common-population and cutoff assumptions are unverified. No adjustment, closure or merged count is assigned. [USDA February letter](https://www.governmentattic.org/6docs/USDAoUnpubCongRpts_2008-2010.pdf#page=16) · [USDA December chart](https://www.governmentattic.org/6docs/USDAoUnpubCongRpts_2008-2010.pdf#page=14) · [House appendix](https://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/200901Majority_Report.pdf#page=15)
+
+## EPA's separate route beyond the tracking list
+
+EPA's revised report **08-P-0123**, March 31, 2008, describes a **January 10, 2008** scope conversation with committee staff. Its foreword and methodology specify a **June 1, 2007** cutoff for the starting list and exclusions including grantee and future-milestone items. DOT's February 29 letter instead describes a **January 15, 2008** criteria letter and an endpoint of **December 17, 2007**. Preserve both dates and selection accounts by recipient. The original DOT-specific criteria and any common instructions remain unacquired. [EPA foreword, physical p. 3, lines 28–34](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=3) · [EPA Appendix A, p. 58, lines 20–44](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=58) · [DOT letter, p. 1](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/DOTOIGOpenRxresponsefeb29.pdf#page=1)
+
+EPA Appendix A says **six** reports appeared as active in individual MATS lookups and were absent from the active report list. It says report **2006-P-00022** had been improperly designated inactive. The review used original agency responses, close-out memoranda and AutoAudit working papers where needed. The foreword explains that a congressional-interest review brought specific recommendations from **2003-P-00012**, EPA's World Trade Center response report, into the revised list. It describes their status as coming from GAO's findings and says full status determination remained in progress. This establishes how EPA said it constructed its list. The comparable DOT selection workpapers and any alternate case-register search remain open. [EPA foreword, physical p. 4, lines 1–9](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=4) · [EPA Appendix A, p. 59, lines 5–22 and 28–46](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=59) · [EPA Appendix B, p. 61, lines 38–39](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=61)
+
+The EPA semiannual report describes **26 reports** in the **February 29** congressional return. The **March 31** revised report says **25 reports / 65 recommendations**, and Appendix B contains **25** distinct IDs. The revised foreword also describes itself as comprised of the information provided to the committee on February 29. Preserve both scopes and counts. The as-sent February packet, actual revision record and row comparison would test whether the reported populations differ and how. The two acquired public URLs for the March revision returned byte-identical PDFs. [EPA semiannual, physical p. 10, printed p. 4, lines 17–26](https://19january2021snapshot.epa.gov/sites/static/files/2015-09/documents/semiannual_report-may_2008.pdf#page=10) · [Revised foreword, pp. 3–4](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=3) · [Appendix B, p. 61](https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2015-11/documents/20080331-08-p-0123-rv.pdf#page=61)
+
+## Scope and next records
+
+The USDA material is an agency response reproduced inside a public release packet. Physical p. 2 describes releasing **23 pages** of responsive records. The hosted PDF has **27 physical pages**, including a publisher cover and release correspondence. Those are separate page-count labels. Reading covered the specified USDA response and table pages, the relevant EPA foreword and method pages and appendix index, and the House method and two agency rows. Source faces were checked where identified in the ledger. Verification rehashed nine saved responses, pinned two held originals, checked 29 anchors and reproduced the cited totals and 25 EPA IDs. The historical House story URL gave HTTP 403 in direct retrieval. The material leaves the original incoming emails, omitted attachments and transport-specific item-level returns open. [Source hashes, scope and locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+- [ ] **PD03–PD04.** Seek the DOT-specific January 15 criteria letter and the incoming December update request. Search the latter by the **December 15, 2008** comparator date, and retain the possibility of a different date or recipient for DOT. Locate the DOT OIG return, any separate Office of the Secretary or audit-liaison output, and the House received-attachment inventory and compilation worksheet.
+- [ ] **PD03–PD04.** Ask of the records whether the two DOT aggregates **168** and **339** include the same reporting population and statuses. Seek the selection/exclusion workpapers and the case-level status ledger using **CC-2006-085** and **042R0122001**, with coverage of investigative recommendations verified independently. Both numbers remain as published. The analogues supply specific tests for coverage. Their agency rules and outcomes are separate from the FAA referral. [DOT February return, p. 1](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/DOTOIGOpenRxresponsefeb29.pdf#page=1) · [House DOT row, p. 15](https://oversight.house.gov/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/200901Majority_Report.pdf#page=15)
+- [ ] **PD01–PD03.** Retain the corrected May 2003 answer and receipt, signed consideration or action/no-action determination, and recommendation-specific implementation and closure records as outstanding. Keep recorded investigative closure separate. [Case-specific record queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/OPEN-RECORDS.md)
